.TH CGC 1 "2026-11-08" "cgc 0.1.0" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
cgc \- clone a Git repository over smart HTTP
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B cgc
[\fIOPTIONS\fR] \fIREPOSITORY\fR [\fIDIRECTORY\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B cgc
is a self-contained implementation of
.BR git-clone (1)
that speaks the Git smart HTTP protocol (version 2) directly.
It downloads the packfile, verifies and unpacks it, resolves deltas, writes
loose objects, refs and configuration, and checks out the working tree with a
Git-compatible index.
.PP
If
.I DIRECTORY
is omitted, the directory name is derived from the repository name, with any
trailing
.B .git
removed.
.SH "REPOSITORY FORMS"
.TP
.B https://\fIhost\fR/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR[.git]
An explicit URL. Plain
.B http://
is accepted for local testing.
.TP
.B gh:\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://github.com/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
.TP
.B gl:\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://gitlab.com/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
.TP
.B bb:\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://bitbucket.org/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
.TP
.B sym:\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://git.symlinx.net/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
.TP
.B \fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://\fIdefault-host\fR/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
The default host is
.B github.com
and can be changed with
.B \-\-host
or
.BR CGC_DEFAULT_HOST .
.TP
.B \fIhost.tld\fR/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR
Expands to
.BR https://\fIhost.tld\fR/\fIowner\fR/\fIrepo\fR.git .
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.B \-\-host \fIhost\fR
Use
.I host
as the default host for the
.IR owner/repo
shorthand.
.TP
.BR \-b ", " \-\-branch " \fIname\fR"
Check out
.I name
(a branch or tag) instead of the remote's default branch. Tags are checked
out in detached HEAD state.
.TP
.B \-\-depth \fIn\fR
Create a shallow clone with history truncated to
.I n
commits. Writes
.B .git/shallow
with the shallow boundary.
.TP
.BR \-q ", " \-\-quiet
Suppress progress messages and status output.
.TP
.BR \-h ", " \-\-help
Print usage information and exit.
.TP
.BR \-V ", " \-\-version
Print the version and exit.
.TP
.B \-\-
Treat all remaining arguments as positional, even if they begin with a dash.
.SH EXAMPLES
.nf
cgc gh:octocat/Hello-World
cgc sym:team/repo
cgc octocat/Hello-World my-copy
cgc https://github.com/torvalds/linux.git
cgc \-\-host git.example.com team/repo
CGC_DEFAULT_HOST=git.example.com cgc team/repo
.fi
.SH OUTPUT
Status is written to standard error in the style of
.BR git-clone (1):
.BR "Cloning into '...'..." ,
any
.B remote:
messages sent by the server, a
.B Receiving objects
download meter,
.BR "Resolving deltas" ,
and
.B Updating files
during checkout.
Live meters are drawn only when standard error is a terminal; final summary
lines are printed when output is redirected.
.SH ENVIRONMENT
.TP
.B CGC_DEFAULT_HOST
Default host used for the
.IR owner/repo
shorthand when
.B \-\-host
is not given.
.SH "EXIT STATUS"
.TP
.B 0
The repository was cloned successfully.
.TP
.B 1
A network, protocol, filesystem, or checkout error occurred.
.TP
.B 2
The command line was invalid.
.SH SAFETY
The remote repository is treated as untrusted. Ref names and
.B HEAD
targets supplied by the server are validated before use, configuration values
are rejected if they contain control characters, and checkout refuses duplicate
paths, file/directory collisions, and paths whose existing parent is a symlink.
This prevents a malicious repository from writing outside the target directory.
These checks are not a sandbox: as with
.BR git-clone (1),
do not run code from an untrusted repository without reviewing it.
.SH LIMITATIONS
No SSH, \fBgit://\fR, or local-path transports; no authentication, so private
repositories are not supported; protocol v2 and SHA-1 only; the whole pack and
all inflated objects are held in memory; no shallow or partial clone, LFS,
hooks, or reflogs.
.SH "SEE ALSO"
.BR git-clone (1),
.BR git-upload-pack (1),
.BR gitprotocol-v2 (5),
.BR git (1)
